BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 270.55 Tm (was wrong: they cut so deep that scaling and growing the business became very difficult, and the build set) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 255.32 Tm (the business back even while saving money [TZp1yBea0o4 @ 00:00:43]. A second utility feed from another) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 240.10 Tm (substation was never an option because only one utility company served the area, so the failover layer big) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 224.87 Tm (colos rely on simply did not exist [TZp1yBea0o4 @ 00:14:42]. Without generators, the only answer to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 209.65 Tm (customers during an outage is that power returns when the utility turns it back on, and cloud buyers already) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 194.42 Tm (assume you sit in a real data center with backup power [TZp1yBea0o4 @ 00:13:34]. Lawrence Systems') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 179.20 Tm (Deft tour shows backup power failing even when you own it: generators run 500 kW to 3 MW each and must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 163.97 Tm (reach speed in about 16 seconds, but if the first unit latches onto the paralleling bus with a bad sine wave,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 148.75 Tm (the others refuse to sync and a site can end up with one of seven generators trying to carry the load) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 133.53 Tm ([gsN_CJJDy_o @ 00:07:08].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 118.30 Tm (Environmental shortcuts kill hardware quietly. Glover warns that running stock air conditioners strips) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 103.08 Tm (moisture, and if humidity lands near 5% you risk a static shock that destroys a ton of hardware, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 87.85 Tm (non-data-center units need bolt-on humidifiers and dehumidifiers [TZp1yBea0o4 @ 00:09:43]. His sharper) Tj ET
