BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 637.77 Tm (Memory is where shared GPUs die first. Julien Semaan's Kubex demo put 5 time-slice replicas on a 24 GB) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 622.55 Tm (L4, and nvidia-smi showed 13 GB for a pod whose real usage was 4 GB, so the standard tool misreported) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 607.32 Tm (who was actually eating the card [Vw7DTM1SV60 @ 00:04:56]. Then a leaky classifier on the same GPU) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 592.10 Tm (pushed LLM A into OOM, killing the well-behaved tenant instead of the offender. The Code Architect traces) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 576.87 Tm (the same failure to layer misalignment: when hardware, driver and orchestration layers disagree, the result) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 561.65 Tm (is OOM errors and node crashes, and Ray's fractional request only sets CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES, letting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 546.42 Tm (PyTorch and vLLM each grab the whole VRAM [TwICQ_zP8Ys @ 00:01:14]. Yuan Chen's GPU-burn) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 531.20 Tm (benchmark quantified the imbalance: under plain time slicing, job 1 took about ten times job 2's memory,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 515.97 Tm (and only MPS with 50% limits evened it out [nOgxv_R13Dg @ 00:23:49]. Dynamia.ai's HAMi talk adds the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 500.75 Tm (utilization cost: without memory isolation, OOM crashes tanked utilization, and reserved memory, 5 GB in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 485.52 Tm (their example, is not the same thing as consumed memory, so unused reservations and noisy neighbors) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 470.30 Tm (both have to be watched [zrGFmLHI7hg @ 00:09:22]. The economics check is blunt: an unenforced fraction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.07 Tm (is an outage waiting for the noisiest neighbor on the card, and it takes down the paying tenant first.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 439.85 Tm (The second trap is capacity that exists on paper but never schedules. Jitesh Powankar frames the baseline) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 424.62 Tm (waste: a pod requesting a whole card may use only 20 to 30 percent, leaving 70 percent idle while other) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 409.40 Tm (pods queue, like booking a whole 50-seat bus for one passenger [Ul1dZowvKvE @ 00:00:34]. DevOps & AI) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 394.17 Tm (Toolkit hit it live on GKE: after llama 2 took the single GPU, the second model sat Pending with no available) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 378.95 Tm (GPUs, and adding another node before the first was at full capacity would have been a waste of money;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 363.72 Tm (recreating the pool with 1g.5gb partitions let up to seven pods share the card [zuRKdveFuZ4 @ 00:08:47].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 348.50 Tm (vCluster's host-cluster walkthrough showed the inverse problem: without time-slicing replicas advertised,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 333.27 Tm (pods simply fail to schedule, so the replica count has to be confirmed on the node before tenants arrive) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 318.05 Tm ([KzJvhbdgvl8 @ 00:04:26]. Gang scheduling is the costliest version: with 8 pods and 4 GPUs, the default) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 302.82 Tm (scheduler places 4 and leaves 4 pending, so the job never starts while 4 GPUs are still consumed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 287.60 Tm ([sXpJ4vSc-cM @ 00:37:13]. DevOps & AI Toolkit also flags the quieter blocker: GPU nodes carry a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.37 Tm (NoSchedule taint, so a pod without the nvidia.com/gpu toleration never lands on the hardware you are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 257.15 Tm (paying for.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 241.92 Tm (The third failure class is drift, and it hits the teams that are already winning. Saiyam warns that deleting the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 226.70 Tm (GPU operator leaves drivers on the node, and a reinstall then produces a version mismatch that just breaks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.47 Tm ([sXpJ4vSc-cM @ 00:01:22]. Luca Berton's air-gapped H200 build lost time to a ConnectX versus Intel) Tj ET
