BT /F2 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 755.00 Tm (THE BIG MONEY PLAYBOOKS) Tj ET
0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Every operator here starts from the same physics: decode is starved by memory, not math. DataMListic lays) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (it out bluntly: each generated token requires reading every weight, so a 70B model streams roughly 140 GB) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (per token while the compute units mostly sit and wait, and batching four requests means one weight load) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (yields four tokens: "Same cost, four times the throughput" [X8CwAqYxH1E @ 00:00:41]. AI WITH Rithesh) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (puts hard numbers on an H100: 80 GB of HBM at 3.35 TB/s against 989 TFLOPS works out to about 295) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (ops per byte, and on a 27B model the compute takes 55 microseconds versus 16 ms of memory reads,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (capping single-user decode near 60 tok/s: "The memory side takes almost 300 times longer" [lasG5MsR-gE) Tj ET
