BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Toll fraud is the loss that lands as a bill nobody in the company placed. Mitel Academy walks the attack) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (paths: stolen SIP trunk credentials registered on a hacker's device, hijacked remote-worker phone) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (credentials, PBX admin logins sniffed or social-engineered to create a rogue extension, voicemail or IVR) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (menus that branch back out to the telco, and call forwarding set to an external destination [ijPHb8SEENo @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (00:07:06]. Their counter-stack is blunt: strip international and long-distance from the dial plan if you never) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (call abroad, ban wildcard patterns because attackers spray random numbers to see which completes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (demand PIN authorization codes for outbound, lock ports 5060 and 5061 to the carrier and known remote) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (IPs, geo-block whole continents, block SIPVicious with an IPS firewall, enable fail-to-ban style lockouts, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (upgrade firmware on PBX and endpoints [ijPHb8SEENo @ 00:10:37]. Sangoma bolts a carrier-side cap on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (top: Fraud Guard sets a maximum weekly international spend, halts international calls when the limit hits,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (and emails a warning as you approach it [dTsrqOzzrOk @ 00:11:02]. VoiceBuy pushes the same logic into) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (the switch, telling buyers to demand that the platform automatically kill active sessions on velocity spikes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (because thin wholesale margins cannot absorb SIM box and international revenue share fraud) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm ([elbBH6g2MU8 @ 00:05:48].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (On the voice-AI side, most breakage is configuration drift rather than carrier failure. Voice AI with Tim says) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (the whitelisted destinations on the Telnyx outbound voice profile tripped them up in the past, warns that a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (Telnyx API key is visible only once and stops working at whatever expiration you set, and stresses that the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (agent name in agent.py must match the dispatch rule exactly or the call has no agent to land on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm ([omQUCQVG1lg @ 00:24:55]. Jonas Massie reports builders get tricked on the Gateway IP field of the Vapi) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (credential request; they route around it by pasting the Twilio termination SIP URI instead of IPv4 ranges) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (because it is much faster and easier [_wo5wokt3dI @ 00:08:47]. Mehmood Feroz names the human) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (bottleneck when bridging a client's existing business number: the incumbent provider has to enable access) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (and whitelist on their side, so you need their support to finish [R74S6hUZ4fk @ 00:04:15]. Omid Mohajerani) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (flags two smaller gotchas: the Vapi trunk username and password should be long, at least around 20) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (characters, and the new BYO trunk may not appear in the dashboard until you refresh the whole page) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm ([HkWcpuMrX7k @ 00:06:53].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (Self-hosted and on-prem stacks break at the network layer first. VisionNLP warns that Azure assigns a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (dynamic public IP that can change while the deployment is live and fail the SIP trunks, so the IP must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (switched to static before the SIP A record goes into Cloudflare with proxy status set to DNS only) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm ([ZQWTIIR9Exs @ 00:05:12]. The same build has to run the SIP service with host networking because SIP) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (and RTP do not work behind Docker's NAT, and even the finished demo carried roughly 400 to 500) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 244.02 Tm (milliseconds of extra lag from a UAE caller dialing a US Telnyx number served by a South India VM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.80 Tm ([ZQWTIIR9Exs @ 00:20:41]. GetVoIP reports that moving voice onto SIP puts much higher bandwidth) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.57 Tm (demand on the network and router, especially with a live call center, which may force a second or more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.35 Tm (powerful router, with QoS settings used to prioritize voice traffic [SUPHe70LM7s @ 00:08:01]. Crosstalk) Tj ET
