BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 443.17 Tm (first click, and treat every bounce as both a fee and a multi-week delay on the client's go-live.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 427.95 Tm (Throughput numbers are where vendors pitch against each other hardest. Will Craig of Signal House quotes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 412.72 Tm (standard limits of 240 SMS segments per minute and 150 MMS per minute on AT&T, and 2,000 segments) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.50 Tm (per day on T-Mobile. Those scale to 4,500 SMS per minute, 2,400 MMS per minute, and 200,000 per day.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.27 Tm (Craig argues that legacy CPaaS providers cap API calls, around 1 per second, which works out to 60) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.05 Tm (messages per minute [sVsWkczKncU @ 00:02:27]. The Signal House tactic is to ask whether a cap is the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 351.82 Tm (carrier rate limit or the provider's internal rate limit. Craig also warns that resellers share one API limit across) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.60 Tm (every customer, which kills speed-to-lead. Telgorithm frames the default tier as 2,000 per day on T-Mobile) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.37 Tm (and 75 TPM on AT&T, with external vetting scores of 80 to 100 unlocking 4,500 TPM and 200,000 per day) Tj ET
